decisions.decision:
Adopt it. Land S/silu.patch (217150e6) without changing its substance. The crate-private feed_forward::silu = evaluate_in_f32(input, activation::silu) goes at every site where a pinned reference calls F.silu / SiLUActivation:
- apply_activation, which covers dense and gated MLPs, routed and shared experts, experiment blocks, T5 gated-silu, and Gemma/Nemotron "silu";
- the attention SiLU output gate;
- the Gated DeltaNet and Mamba-2 convolution SiLU.
ClampedSwiGlu stays composed operation by operation, because gpt-oss's reference is gate * torch.sigmoid(gate * alpha). The gated norms keep their existing F32 SiLU. F32 and F64 stay bit-identical to Burn's graph.
Ordering: commit it after the envelope harness of (b)/(c), so no head ever judges it under the 1.2/0.5 rules. Before the branch is offered for integration, re-qualify the advertised Qwen3.5-0.8B Metal/F16 profile: parity, memory, and the v0.1 benchmark.

Calibrate F16 the same way as BF16, on the official F16 graphs:
- add float16 to the generator;
- generate the four F16 graphs per truth, with decode and prompt-decode rows;
- derive F16's own leave-one-out slacks by the same procedure;
- retire the BF16-as-upper-limit proxy.

If any official F16 graph of a prompt is non-finite, that checkpoint has no F16 envelope. Its F16 gates then fail as "uncalibrated: the reference is non-finite in F16" and never pass.

On current measurements this reclassifies Qwen2-7B Metal/F16 as uncalibrated: official CPU and MPS F16 eager are NaN on every prompt. Its decode deviation is recorded as a finding to diagnose before any F16 claim.
